# Remaining work

Built features are documented under docs/ — see docs/requirements.md for the
requirement -> implementation map. This file lists only what is NOT done.

## Verify on a live Proxmox host
Everything was built and tested offline (`worms test`); no node was available.
The standing caveat and the first live steps are in docs/testing.md.
- A full round and a full devbox lifecycle on a real node: VM/bridge creation,
  the devbox `-replace` rebuild, the SSH-gateway `permitopen` confinement, and
  `worms simulate`.
- Attach the port-isolation hookscript (needs root@pam; it is wired through
  every VM module but left commented — docs/security-assessment.md, S4).

## Security hardening
Tracked in docs/security-assessment.md ("not done"): a per-account login
lockout (D3; per-address rate limiting is done), team-join consent (D4),
current-password on a voluntary change (D5); Proxmox provider TLS
verification (C1); and locking devpi and the Docker registry to
read-only/authenticated before re-enabling them (S2).

## Not yet built
- A dashboard design pass (the worm upload flow and the contract are
  documented now -- docs/worm-contract.md).
- Heartbeat: define the "vital" services per VM, a collector, and its DB schema.
- GPU / inference-engine service (jailbreaking scenarios).
- Richer sandbox topology generation: L2/L3 switches and seeded vulnerabilities.
- Private-internet services exist as Ansible roles but are disabled in the
  stack (only Wikipedia is deployed); re-enable apt-cache / devpi / registry /
  manpages / cve-search once locked down (S2).
